  "assertions": [
    {
      "name": "a_proton_proton_bond_is_exactly_one_markov_reduction",
      "computed": true,
      "expected": true,
      "passed": true,
      "note": "b_pp = z is a derived identity, so log_z b_pp = 1 on the nose. The tower's own structure map counts p-p bonds exactly"
    },
    {
      "name": "all_five_factors_equal_z_exactly_at_q_equals_one",
      "computed": true,
      "expected": true,
      "passed": true,
      "note": "the Hecke algebra degenerates to C[S_n] and z(1) = 1/2, so nu becomes an exact integer bond count -- verified symbolically, not numerically"
    },
    {
      "name": "the_pn_interface_has_no_first_order_term",
      "computed": true,
      "expected": true,
      "passed": true,
      "note": "and b_pp, b_nn split symmetrically at +1 and -1 -- the whole isospin structure is one sign, at first order in q-1"
    },
    {
      "name": "like_species_bonds_split_symmetrically_about_z",
      "computed": true,
      "expected": true,
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "first_order_expansion_is_good_to_four_percent",
      "computed": true,
      "expected": true,
      "passed": true,
      "note": "so the order-0 + order-1 picture is the whole law to 4 %"
    },
    {
      "name": "layout_free_bond_counting_beats_every_isospin_resolved_variant",
      "computed": true,
      "expected": true,
      "passed": true,
      "note": "1.18085 vs best isospin-resolved 1.22497 -- the q-deformation's contribution to the binding law is net-NEGATIVE"
    },
    {
      "name": "the_three_edge_sets_agree_to_within_one_percent",
      "computed": true,
      "expected": true,
      "passed": true,
      "note": "so the nucleon-ordering gap (qou-48is), real for tr_M at 20-36 %, barely touches B"
    },
    {
      "name": "the_derived_asymmetry_has_the_wrong_sign",
      "computed": true,
      "expected": true,
      "passed": true,
      "note": "derived +0.2200, data wants ~-0.15. My earlier reading of b_pp > b_nn as 'the sign Coulomb would give' is correct as ALGEBRA and wrong as EVIDENCE. RETRACTED"
    },
    {
      "name": "the_missing_term_is_the_symmetry_energy_not_the_surface_term",
      "computed": true,
      "expected": true,
      "passed": true,
      "note": "|corr| 0.8038 vs 0.1781 -- the decision frame named the surface term / edge set as the strongest lead. Wrong by 4x in correlation. But the isospin/SU(4) route (qou-ubsl) is a COMPLETED bean, closed by this arc's own row cap -- so this is a named gap with NO route, not a lead. Corrected same day"
    },
    {
      "name": "binding_information_is_gone_from_Delta_tr_by_mass_eleven",
      "computed": true,
      "expected": true,
      "passed": true,
      "note": "above A ~ 11 Delta_tr does not merely MIS-SCALE the binding energy, it does not CONTAIN it -- what is left is t_p^Z t_n^N. That is why no scale works"
    }
  ],
